WEBVTT

00:00.320 --> 00:01.890
- [Voiceover] So we have a trapezoid here

00:01.890 --> 00:04.510
on the coordinate plane
and what we want to do is

00:04.510 --> 00:08.652
find the area of this trapezoid,
just given this diagram.

00:08.652 --> 00:10.120
And, like always, pause this video and see

00:10.120 --> 00:11.879
if you can figure it out.

00:11.879 --> 00:14.271
Well, we know how to figure
out the area of a trapezoid.

00:14.271 --> 00:16.924
We have videos where
we derive this formula.

00:16.924 --> 00:19.246
But, the area of a
trapezoid, just put simply,

00:19.246 --> 00:23.777
is equal to the average of
the lengths of the bases,

00:23.777 --> 00:27.944
we could say base one plus
base two times the height.

00:29.285 --> 00:31.846
And, so what are our bases here?

00:31.846 --> 00:35.106
What are, and what is going
to be our height over here?

00:35.106 --> 00:38.139
Well, we could call base one,

00:38.139 --> 00:40.346
we could call that segment CL,

00:40.346 --> 00:43.268
so it would be the length of
segment CL, right over here.

00:43.268 --> 00:45.169
I'll do that in magenta.

00:45.169 --> 00:47.207
That is going to be base one.

00:47.207 --> 00:49.790
Base two, base two, that could,

00:51.290 --> 00:53.117
we'll do that in a different color.

00:53.117 --> 00:56.700
Base two would be the
length of segment OW,

00:58.577 --> 00:59.748
or b two would be the length

00:59.748 --> 01:03.011
of segment OW, right over there.

01:03.011 --> 01:06.526
And then, our height, our height h,

01:06.526 --> 01:07.759
well, that would just be an altitude

01:07.759 --> 01:09.739
and they did one in a dotted line, here.

01:09.739 --> 01:12.449
Notice it intersects the, base one,

01:12.449 --> 01:15.918
I guess you could say segment
CL at a right angle, here.

01:15.918 --> 01:19.188
And so, this would be,
this would be the height.

01:19.188 --> 01:21.416
So, if we know the
lengths of each of these,

01:21.416 --> 01:22.847
if we know each of these values,

01:22.847 --> 01:24.480
which are the lengths of these segments,

01:24.480 --> 01:28.349
then we can evaluate the area
of this actual trapezoid.

01:28.349 --> 01:30.838
And, once again, if this is
completely unfamiliar to you

01:30.838 --> 01:32.418
or of you're curious,
we have multiple videos

01:32.418 --> 01:33.518
talking about the proofs

01:33.518 --> 01:35.788
or how we came up with this formula.

01:35.788 --> 01:37.878
You an even break out,
break down a trapezoid

01:37.878 --> 01:39.269
into two triangles and a rectangle,

01:39.269 --> 01:40.965
which is one way to think about it.

01:40.965 --> 01:43.334
Anyway, let's see how we
could figure this out.

01:43.334 --> 01:45.694
So, the first one is,
what is b one going to be?

01:45.694 --> 01:48.444
B one is the length of segment CL

01:49.575 --> 01:53.906
and you could say, "We'll
look, we know what these,

01:53.906 --> 01:55.876
"the coordinates of these points are."

01:55.876 --> 01:57.922
You could say, "Let's use
the distance formula,"

01:57.922 --> 01:59.307
and you could say, "Well,
the distance formula is just

01:59.307 --> 02:01.618
"an application of the
Pythagorean Theorem."

02:01.618 --> 02:02.907
So, this is going to be

02:02.907 --> 02:06.477
the square root of our
change in x squared,

02:06.477 --> 02:09.258
so our change in x is going
to be this, right over here.

02:09.258 --> 02:11.056
And, notice, we're going
from x equals negative four

02:11.056 --> 02:13.928
to x equals eight, as w go from C to L.

02:13.928 --> 02:18.095
So, our change in x is equal
to eight minus negative four

02:20.250 --> 02:22.700
which is equal to 12.

02:22.700 --> 02:26.299
And, our change in in y, our change in y,

02:26.299 --> 02:30.290
we are going from y equals
negative one to y equals five.

02:30.290 --> 02:32.478
So, we could say our change in y

02:32.478 --> 02:35.828
equal to five minus negative one

02:35.828 --> 02:37.189
which, of course, is equal to six.

02:37.189 --> 02:41.450
And, you see that: one,
two, three, four, five, six.

02:41.450 --> 02:43.299
And, the segment that we care about,

02:43.299 --> 02:46.268
its length that we care about,
that's just the hypotenuse

02:46.268 --> 02:48.909
of this right triangle
that has one side 12

02:48.909 --> 02:50.687
and one side six.

02:50.687 --> 02:52.209
So, the length of that hypotenuse,

02:52.209 --> 02:53.942
from the Pythagorean Theorem,

02:53.942 --> 02:55.770
and, as I mentioned,
the distance formula is

02:55.770 --> 02:58.091
just an application of
the Pythagorean Theorem,

02:58.091 --> 02:59.724
this is going to be

02:59.724 --> 03:02.664
our change in x, squared, 12 squared,

03:02.664 --> 03:06.074
plus our change in y,
squared, so plus six squared,

03:06.074 --> 03:09.221
and this is going to be
equal to 144 plus 36.

03:09.221 --> 03:12.054
So, the square root of 144 plus 36

03:13.983 --> 03:16.816
is one hundred, one hundred and 80

03:18.079 --> 03:22.964
which is equal to, let's
see, 180 is 36 times five.

03:22.964 --> 03:27.131
So, that is six square roots,
six square roots of five.

03:28.770 --> 03:30.332
Oh, let me not skip some steps.

03:30.332 --> 03:33.901
So, this is the square
root of 36 times five

03:33.901 --> 03:36.577
which is equal to, square root of 36 is 6,

03:36.577 --> 03:38.910
so six square roots of five.

03:40.350 --> 03:42.950
Now, let's figure out b two.

03:42.950 --> 03:46.759
So, b two, once again, change in x squared

03:46.759 --> 03:48.828
plus the square root
of change in x squared

03:48.828 --> 03:50.418
plus change in y squared.

03:50.418 --> 03:53.068
Well, let's see, if we're going from,

03:53.068 --> 03:55.298
we could set up a right
triangle, if you like,

03:55.298 --> 03:58.279
like this, to figure those things out.

03:58.279 --> 04:02.446
So, our change in x, we're
going from x is at negative two,

04:03.889 --> 04:07.000
x is going from negative
two to positive four.

04:07.000 --> 04:09.036
So, our change in x is six.

04:09.036 --> 04:11.953
Our change in y, we are going from,

04:13.958 --> 04:18.125
we are going from y equals, y
equals five to y equals eight.

04:20.048 --> 04:23.139
So, our change in y is equal to three.

04:23.139 --> 04:25.217
So, just applying the Pythagorean Theorem

04:25.217 --> 04:27.055
to find the length of
the hypotenuse, here,

04:27.055 --> 04:28.209
is going to be the square root

04:28.209 --> 04:31.109
of change in x squared, six squared,

04:31.109 --> 04:34.176
plus change in y squared,
plus three squared

04:34.176 --> 04:36.213
which is going to be equal to,

04:36.213 --> 04:39.463
it's going to be equal to 36 plus nine,

04:42.780 --> 04:45.613
which is 45, so, square root of 45

04:47.580 --> 04:50.948
which is equal to the square
root of nine times five

04:50.948 --> 04:55.501
which is equal to three
square roots of five.

04:55.501 --> 04:56.990
And so, we only have
one left to figure out.

04:56.990 --> 04:58.717
We have to figure out h.

04:58.717 --> 05:01.889
We have to figure out the length of h.

05:01.889 --> 05:05.128
So, h is going to be equal to,

05:05.128 --> 05:07.860
and so, what is our, if
we're going from W to N,

05:07.860 --> 05:09.810
our change in x is two.

05:09.810 --> 05:11.520
Change in x is equal to two.

05:11.520 --> 05:14.790
We're going from X equals
four to x equals six.

05:14.790 --> 05:16.141
If you want to do that purely numerically,

05:16.141 --> 05:17.940
we would say, "Okay, our
endpoint, our x value is six.

05:17.940 --> 05:19.351
"Our starting point, our x-value is four.

05:19.351 --> 05:21.400
"Six minus four is two."

05:21.400 --> 05:22.790
You see that visually, here.

05:22.790 --> 05:24.601
So, it's going to be the square root

05:24.601 --> 05:26.968
of two squared plus our,

05:26.968 --> 05:29.771
let me write that radical
a little bit better.

05:29.771 --> 05:33.090
So, it's the square root
of our change in x squared

05:33.090 --> 05:35.318
plus our change in y squared.

05:35.318 --> 05:38.002
Our change in y is negative four.

05:38.002 --> 05:40.031
Change in y is negative four

05:40.031 --> 05:41.410
but we're going to square it,

05:41.410 --> 05:43.428
so it's going to become a positive 16.

05:43.428 --> 05:44.750
So, this is going to be equal

05:44.750 --> 05:46.602
to the square root of four plus 16.

05:46.602 --> 05:48.102
Square root of 20,

05:49.220 --> 05:53.490
which is equal to the square
root of four times five,

05:53.490 --> 05:55.992
which is equal to two times
the square root of five.

05:55.992 --> 05:58.221
It's nice that the square
root of five keeps popping up.

05:58.221 --> 05:59.240
And so, now we just substitute

05:59.240 --> 06:01.042
into our original expression.

06:01.042 --> 06:04.731
And so, our Area of our
trapezoid is going to be

06:04.731 --> 06:08.719
one half times six square roots of five,

06:08.719 --> 06:10.800
six square roots of five,

06:10.800 --> 06:13.319
plus three square roots of five,

06:13.319 --> 06:16.530
plus three square roots of five,

06:16.530 --> 06:18.501
let me close that parentheses,

06:18.501 --> 06:20.819
times two square roots of five,

06:20.819 --> 06:24.021
times two square roots of five.

06:24.021 --> 06:26.401
And, let's see how we can simplify this.

06:26.401 --> 06:27.411
So, six square roots of five

06:27.411 --> 06:28.450
plus three square roots of five,

06:28.450 --> 06:32.021
that is nine square roots of five.

06:32.021 --> 06:33.840
Let's see, the one half times the two,

06:33.840 --> 06:35.811
those cancel out to just be one.

06:35.811 --> 06:36.644
And so, we're left with

06:36.644 --> 06:39.387
nine square roots of five
times the square root of five.

06:39.387 --> 06:40.838
Well, the square root of five
times the square root of five

06:40.838 --> 06:43.198
is just going to be five.

06:43.198 --> 06:45.996
So, this is equal to nine times five

06:45.996 --> 06:50.163
which is equal to 45 square
units or units squared.
